1
00:00:00,478 --> 00:00:03,579
Hi everyone! Today I'm presenting IncidentLens,

2
00:00:04,068 --> 00:00:08,340
an evidence-driven multi-agent system for
software incident root cause analysis.

3
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:14,080
In production postmortems, the most dangerous
failure mode isn't failing to find an answer —

4
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,060
it's hallucinating a plausible
story. Generic LLM agents

5
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:22,334
routinely assert confident root
causes without valid citations,

6
00:00:22,829 --> 00:00:27,291
ignore data access boundaries, and almost
never admit when evidence is missing.

7
00:00:27,503 --> 00:00:31,091
IncidentLens enforces a much
stricter engineering contract:

8
00:00:31,514 --> 00:00:35,220
every claim must cite an
actually observed evidence ID,

9
00:00:35,716 --> 00:00:39,120
every agent operates inside
explicit read-only tool permissions,

10
00:00:39,756 --> 00:00:43,451
and when visible telemetry cannot
uniquely identify the root cause,

11
00:00:43,931 --> 00:00:47,678
the system must abstain with
INCONCLUSIVE rather than guess.

12
00:00:48,086 --> 00:00:50,855
Over the next nine minutes,
I'll walk through the architecture,

13
00:00:51,241 --> 00:00:54,963
show you four live hands-on demos,
and share our full-scale,

14
00:00:55,219 --> 00:00:59,393
cross-model experimental findings
across DeepSeek and Tencent Hunyuan.
